#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""La minuterie (story 113, cycle 59; a hook, a law of the story stated in line 1, an escalation through the whole country, a reversal, a dry last line).
This man lives on the seventh floor and the stairwell's light timer lasts thirty seconds: he never gets home before the dark. He hires a coach, until
the evening he has light all the way to his door. The landlord finds that too long and sets fifteen seconds; he keeps up, five steps a stride.
Champions come to train in his stairwell and the landlord charges at the door; a short timer is a gym at home, rents double, every landlord in the
country shortens his; grandparents move into the hall, removal men run pianos up the stairs and win the world stair championship. His timer now
lasts one second. Yesterday he twisted his ankle on the third floor and sat in the dark. Above his head there was a button. There is one on every floor.
Running gag (never said): a glowing orange timer button on every landing (mnButtons: a pale plate, an orange ring, a lit cap and a soft orange glow
that faces the camera, on the front face of the newel column at the well's end, 2.05 m up: out of the old lady's reach, so she goes on tiptoe), and
the neighbour du troisième (tiny, grey bun, purple coat, tartan trolley) presses it on every landing with one finger, deadpan, never looking, never
hurrying, always in her own warm light (a darkPool that follows her when the stairwell is dark): S02 (two floors under his blackout), S04 (crossing the
hall), S05b (one step, one button), S06 (the champions blow past her), S09b (the button at the foot of the stairs, after a polite nod to the
grandparents, the same age), S10b (the piano gust), S12b (lit alone when his one second runs out), S14b (her pool climbing the dark flight), S15
(above his head). The hero only ever slaps the big button by the front door (S01, S03, S12b): he knows what a button is, he never looks up. S01b
already shows the column of small orange glows up the well, off the middle; S16 shows them big, centred, seven dots stacked into the distance. By
ear « dure trente secondes » (L01) comes back as « dure une seconde » (L12), « avant le noir » (L02) as « dans le noir » (L14), « au septième » (L01)
as « à chaque étage » (L16).
Staging (natural look; one new set for twelve lines: mnStairwell, a cutaway of seven floors over the ground floor hall, front open, with a lit state and
a deep blue dark state; a cut every 0.7 to 2.0 s, long lines split on their words, every cut just under its frame):
S01 the hall at night, deep blue: his eyes and the big orange button glow; he winds up and slaps it without looking (squash, hair up), the light
comes on, a determined frown, a crouch, and he is gone (a dashed hole of speed, mnGhost). S01b up the well from its foot: the landings stacked like a
telescope, a column of small orange glows low on the right; his footsteps race up. S02 the cutaway, floors three to five: he sprints up the flights,
skids on the fifth landing, turns to us, and the light cuts on « noir »: deep blue, pale lines on the steps' noses and the rails (mnDarkLines), only
his eyes, two blinks; two floors down the neighbour presses her button in her own warm pool. S02b the next evening in the hall: a coach in a plain blue
tracksuit blows his whistle and holds up a stopwatch with hands only; the hero, ankle weights over his trousers, skips with his tie (the red cord swung
round him, his own tie hidden), hops with a stretch up and a squash down. S03 the hall, lower and closer: the slap, the crouch, gone. S03b the seventh
landing: he skids in, his arm shoots out like rubber to the lock, the key turns; he turns to us and pumps both fists, a hop, a huge grin (VICTOIRE);
on « porte » the light cuts: the grin and the eyes hang in the dark. S04 the hall: the landlord (thin, grey suit, mustard tie, round glasses,
clipboard) opens the grey timer box (a dial, one hand, six ticks, a pale bar, no digit), frowns at it, frowns at us, ticks his clipboard; behind him
the neighbour crosses the hall with her trolley. S04b close on the dial: two fingers turn the knob, the hand snaps to half, CLIC. S05 one flight from
the front: he takes it in one stride, legs scissored across the frame, a squash on the half landing. S05b the next flight, the camera rising; below,
the neighbour climbs one step and presses her landing's button. S06 the fourth landing: three champions in plain coloured kits sprint past her, the
gusts shake her, she presses, deadpan. S06b the hall: the champions queue bouncing and stretching; the landlord tears blank tickets off a roll, plain
gold coins fly into his breast pocket, KA-CHING, a smirk. S07 the first landing dressed as a gym (a towel over the banister, a bottle on the bottom
step): the landlord sweeps his arm at the stairs for a young couple in tracksuits. S07b the young man does step-ups on the bottom step, the young woman
jogs on the spot, the landlord spreads his hands. S07c low over the doormat: a second stack of plain gold coins pops up coin by coin beside the first;
the couple gasp, mouths like letterboxes. S08 three grey boxes high on a wall: three rubber arms rise from below and turn three dials down at once,
CLIC. S08b a street at night, every window dark: in each block a strip of stairwell windows blinks on and off, out of step, like fairy lights. S09 the
hall by the blank letterboxes: grandpa reads the paper (columns and a picture, no word) sitting up in a single bed, grandma waters a geranium, an
armchair, a standard lamp. S09b the neighbour crosses the hall, she and grandpa nod politely, she presses the button at the foot of the stairs. S10 the
cutaway from the front: two removal men run an upright piano up a flight, legs a blur, the piano wobbling. S10b the fourth landing: the piano blows
past the neighbour; once it is gone she presses, deadpan. S11 the top landing (no banner, no name, no flag): the movers burst in first and drop the
piano, BOUM, and cheer; two champions arrive a beat later, bent double, panting. S11b a three-step podium (heights and colours only): the movers share
the top step, each biting a plain gold disc on a mustard ribbon, the champions sour on the lower steps (PODIUM). S12 low under the box: the knob turned
all the way down, the hand slams onto the last tick, CLAC. S12b the hall: the slap, he is gone (a dashed hole of speed, his briefcase left spinning in
the air); one second later the light goes out: the neighbour stays in her own light, the briefcase drops in the dark. S13 the third landing in the dark:
he races up and round the column, his foot folds like rubber, he pitches over and lands sitting on the first step; high and in front, the frame keeps
the wall above his head out. S13b his ankle swells like a balloon (the shoe kept in the frame), his briefcase comes down from the dark onto his head,
BONK, spinning eyes, stars. S14 from the other side, still deep blue: only his white eyes, glancing left, right, left; a far clanking. S14b down the
dark flight from the landing: a warm pool climbs toward us one step at a time, the neighbour and her trolley, clank, clank. S15 wider: she arrives,
goes up on her toes and, without looking at him, presses the glowing button right above his head: the light floods back. S15b close and low: his eyes
go up to the button, his jaw drops. S16 up the well again, square on the column: seven big orange dots stacked up the middle of the frame into the
distance, all lit, a click each. S16b the landing: he turns his head from the button to us, deadpan, one blink; she is already a step further up the
next flight, her trolley bumping after her. Hold.
Props (engine/props_minuterie.js, cycle 59): mnStairwell, mnButtons, mnDarkLines, mnTimerBox, mnTrolley, mnClipboard, mnTicketRoll, mnCoins, mnTowel,
mnBottle, mnDoormat, mnPiano, mnPodium, mnMedal, mnAnkleWeight, mnSwollen, mnTieRope, mnGhost, mnStrips, mnFloorLamp, mnGeranium, mnPaper, mnKey;
reused: briefcase, whistle, stopwatch (hands and ticks only), bed, wateringCan, speedLines (props.js), armchair (props_ascenseur), plainWall
(props_ombre); sets whiteVoid (the stairwell is a prop), parisStreet (night, windows off, no
Eiffel tower). Never the elevator (a digital floor display), never the medal prop (a tricolour ribbon), never immeubleCoupe (no flights).
Lessons applied from the start: Looney deformation on every accent (the slaps, the crouches and the dashes, the stride's scissors and its landing
squash, the skip's stretch and squash, the rubber arm to the lock, the victory hops, the gasp, the stretched arms of the three landlords, the trip,
the balloon ankle, the bonk); every action starts in the first 0.3 s of its shot; one take for the hero at the twist only (S15b: eyes up, jaw drops),
the others react with frowns, smirks, gasps and nods; blinks and breathing on holds (life()); no raised arm held still (fists pump, the landlord's arm
sweeps, the coach's watch arm bent); carried props are world props or attached with `hang` (briefcase), the hands guided on their grip (the trolley's
handle, the clipboard, the ticket roll, the paper); look targets at head height or the camera, pupils for the rest; word timings from timeline.json
through st.at (words from 0, printed beside their times); every cut set just under its frame (floor(round(t*30)/30*1e4)/1e4); cameras fitted with
fit()/fitBack() or placed by a small grid search, all checked with project() at their start and end (CHECKS and BANDS: heads out of the caption band
0.77-0.83 and, under a card, out of the card band 0.07-0.18); the dark is the scene's dark grade with a high floor and a blue tint (deep blue, never
black), the eyes of the face rig, pale lines and the buttons drawn inDark, the neighbour's warm darkPool, a faint orange pool from the button over his
head; the set casts no shadow (stacked slabs would black out every floor below) and every surface laid on another is 2 cm proud or more (tiles, door
frames, dots, the lines of the dark); at most five people per shot; floors counted by landings and rows of painted dots, never by a number; no clock,
dial or podium with a digit; no brand, logo, flag, emblem, cross, insignia or currency on screen; plain tracksuits and kits (no stripe, no number);
French only (VICTOIRE, PODIUM are the cards; no other word on screen); the satire aims at the absurd rule of the timer and at the one landlord, never at
a group; nobody hurt beyond a cartoon ankle."""
from story_kit import *
import math

st = Story('minuterie', look='natural')
st.plan([('S01', 'L01', 0), ('S01b', 'L01', 5), ('S02', 'L02', 0), ('S02b', 'L02', 6), ('S03', 'L03', 0), ('S03b', 'L03', 2), ('S04', 'L04', 0), ('S04b', 'L04', 7),
         ('S05', 'L05', 0), ('S05b', 'L05', 4), ('S06', 'L06', 0), ('S06b', 'L06', 6), ('S07', 'L07', 0), ('S07b', 'L07', 3), ('S07c', 'L07', 10),
         ('S08', 'L08', 0), ('S08b', 'L08', 5), ('S09', 'L09', 0), ('S09b', 'L09', 3), ('S10', 'L10', 0), ('S10b', 'L10', 4), ('S11', 'L11', 0), ('S11b', 'L11', 5),
         ('S12', 'L12', 0), ('S12b', 'L12', 3), ('S13', 'L13', 0), ('S13b', 'L13', 5), ('S14', 'L14', 0), ('S14b', 'L14', 7), ('S15', 'L15', 0), ('S15b', 'L15', 4),
         ('S16', 'L16', 0), ('S16b', 43.0, 0)])
# every cut just under its frame: st.cut rounds to 4 decimals (53/30 -> 1.7667, after the frame: its first image would show the shot before); take the
# frame index and floor its time instead
FL = lambda v: math.floor(round(v * 30) / 30 * 10000) / 10000
st.SH = {sid: (FL(a), FL(b) if b < st.total else b) for sid, (a, b) in st.SH.items()}

PI = math.pi
def r(v, n=3): return round(v, n)
def add(a, b): return [r(a[i] + b[i]) for i in range(3)]
def lerp3(a, b, u): return [r(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u) for i in range(3)]
def yaw(src, dst): return r(math.degrees(math.atan2(dst[0] - src[0], dst[2] - src[2])), 1)
def fwd(ry): return [math.sin(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.cos(math.radians(ry))]
def right(ry): return [-math.cos(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.sin(math.radians(ry))]
def off(p, ry, f=0.0, s=0.0, y=0.0): F, R = fwd(ry), right(ry); return [r(p[0] + F[0] * f + R[0] * s), r(p[1] + y), r(p[2] + F[2] * f + R[2] * s)]
CHECKS = []
def chk(sid, frm, look, lens, pts, heads=(), card=False):
    pr = {n: project(frm, look, lens, p) for n, p in pts.items()}
    CHECKS.append(f"{sid}: " + ' | '.join(f"{n} {v}" for n, v in pr.items()))
    for n in heads:
        v = pr.get(n)
        if not v or not (0.0 <= v[0] <= 1.0 and 0.0 <= v[1] <= 1.0): CHECKS.append(f"  BANDS {sid}: {n} out of the frame {v}")
        elif 0.765 <= v[1] <= 0.835: CHECKS.append(f"  BANDS {sid}: {n} in the caption band {v}")
        elif card and 0.07 <= v[1] <= 0.18: CHECKS.append(f"  BANDS {sid}: {n} in the card band {v}")
def chkc(sid, c, pts, heads=(), end=False, card=False):
    frm, look = (c.get('to') or c['from'], c.get('lookAt2') or c['lookAt']) if end else (c['from'], c['lookAt'])
    chk(sid + ('>' if end else ''), frm, look, c['lens'], pts, heads, card)
def chk2(sid, c, pts, heads=(), card=False): chkc(sid, c, pts, heads, card=card); chkc(sid, c, pts, heads, end=True, card=card)
def W(sid, lid, i):
    # word timings from timeline.json: st.at counts the words from 0; the word is printed beside its time
    t = st.at(sid, lid, i); CHECKS.append(f"{sid} « {st.L[lid]['words'][i]['w']} » at {t}"); return t
def R5(p, w=1, s=0.0): return [*p, w, s]
def FIT(frm, pts, back=False, **kw):
    # the aim and the lens that hold every point (heads with a margin of the width, above the captions): fit() / fitBack() of the kit
    kw.setdefault('margin', 0.14); kw.setdefault('top', 0.1); kw.setdefault('bottom', 0.75); kw.setdefault('lenses', range(28, 60))
    if back: f, look, lens = fitBack(frm, pts, **kw)
    else:
        f = frm; look, lens, _ = fit(frm, pts, **{k_: v for k_, v in kw.items() if k_ not in ('inside', 'level')})
        if not lens: f, look, lens = fitBack(frm, pts, **kw)
    assert lens, f'no lens fits from {frm}'
    return [r(v) for v in f], [r(v) for v in look], lens
def HAND(R=None, L=None, hr='rest', hl='rest', tipR=0.0, tipL=0.0, **x):
    return {'reach': {**({'R': R5(R, 1, tipR)} if R else {}), **({'L': R5(L, 1, tipL)} if L else {})}, 'hands': {'R': hr, 'L': hl}, 'hip': 0, **x}
def blink(t, face, keep=None): return [k(t, toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': {**face, 'lid': 1.0}}, toonDur=0.05), k(r(t + 0.1), toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': face}, toonDur=0.06)]
def life(t0, t1, face, keep=None, ph=0.0, blinks=(), period=0.9, amp=0.013):
    # a moving hold: slow breathing keys that carry the face and the hands (a toon key is a whole state), clear of the blinks
    out, bl, t_, i = [], sorted(blinks), t0 + ph, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.1:
        if not any(-0.04 < t_ - b < 0.2 for b in bl):
            q = [r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4), r(1 + amp, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4)] if i % 2 == 0 else [r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.6, 4), r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4)]
            out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'sq': q, 'face': face}, toonDur=r(period * 0.8), toonEase='inOut'))
        t_ += period / 2; i += 1
    for b in bl: out += blink(r(b), face, keep)
    return out

# ============================== the stairwell (engine/props_minuterie.js, mnStairwell: its numbers are in the prop's header)
FH = 2.8; BH = 2.05; G = 0.02; DOORX = 2.9
def LAND(k_, x=2.2, z=0.0): return [x, r(FH * k_ + (G if k_ == 0 else 0.0)), z]
def STA(k_, i, z=0.97): return [r(1.225 - 0.35 * i), r(FH * k_ + 0.175 * (i + 1)), z]
def STB(k_, i, z=-0.97): return [r(-1.225 + 0.35 * i), r(FH * k_ + 1.4 + 0.175 * (i + 1)), z]
def HALF(k_, x=-2.1, z=0.0): return [x, r(FH * k_ + 1.4), z]
def BTN(k_): return [1.26, r(FH * k_ + BH), 0.2]
BIG = [5.05, 1.35, -1.45]
LOCK7 = [2.54, r(FH * 7 + 1.05), -1.4]
SET = 'whiteVoid'; SETO = {'color': '#E7E1D3'}
DARK = {'darkFloor': 0.42, 'darkTint': '#5F86E0', 'darkEyes': 2.4}
LOOK_IN = {'exposure': 1.0}
def WELL(n, **o): return P(f'cage{n}', 'mnStairwell', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts=o)
def BTNS(n, **o): return P(f'boutons{n}', 'mnButtons', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts=o, inDark=True)
def LINES(n, on=None, off_=None, **o):
    # the pale lines of the dark (inDark): shown from `on` (s) until `off_`
    ks = [k(0.0, visible=on is not None and on <= 0.0)]
    if on is not None and on > 0: ks.append(k(on, visible=True))
    if off_ is not None: ks.append(k(off_, visible=False))
    return P(f'traits{n}', 'mnDarkLines', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts=o, inDark=True, keys=ks)
def BRIEF(n, who='mec'): return P(f'mallette{n}', 'briefcase', on={'actor': who, 'hand': 'L', 'hang': True})
def NOSHADOW(pid, who): return P(pid, 'poNoShadow', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts={'who': who})

# the neighbour's trolley: it trails behind her, its -Z side to her, tipped back by TT (rad); handle(p, ry) is where its handle is
TT = -0.32
def handle(p, ry, tilt=TT):
    # the handle sits 0.98 up and 0.08 behind the axle in the trolley's frame; the trolley faces away from her (ry + 180)
    y = 0.98 * math.cos(tilt) + 0.08 * math.sin(tilt); zl = 0.98 * math.sin(tilt) - 0.08 * math.cos(tilt)
    F = fwd(ry + 180); return [r(p[0] + F[0] * zl), r(p[1] + y), r(p[2] + F[2] * zl)]
def TROLLEY(n, p, ry, keys=None, bump=None, tilt=TT):
    return P(f'caddie{n}', 'mnTrolley', pos=list(p), ry=r(ry + 180, 1), rot=[tilt, 0, 0], rotOrder='YXZ', opts={**({'bump': bump} if bump else {})}, **({'keys': keys} if keys else {}))
VF = {'lid': 0.45, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.0}

GAGS = []
def GAG(*a): GAGS.append(a)

# ============================== the hero: a briefcase in his left mitten; HF his face
HF = {'lid': 0.35, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.1}
HFD = {'lid': 0.0, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': -0.5, 'eye': 0.2}         # determined
def SPLAT_FACE(**x): return {**HF, 'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.4, 'brow': 0.9, **x}

# 1: « Ce mec habite au septième. » The hall at night, deep blue: only his eyes and the big orange button by the front door glow; he winds his right arm
#    up high and slaps the button without looking (a squash, his hair jolts): the light comes on at the slap; he turns to us, a determined frown, crouches
#    and shoots off toward the stairs (a dashed hole of speed where he stood)
D1 = st.dur('S01'); SLAP1 = 0.3; GO1 = 0.74
H1 = [5.62, G, -1.0]; RY1 = -55
WIND1 = off(H1, RY1, 0.1, 0.4, 2.45); HIT1 = add(BIG, [0.0, 0.0, 0.08])
F1, L1, LN1 = FIT([3.75, 0.9, 2.95], {'head': add(H1, [0, 2.4, 0]), 'feet': add(H1, [0, 0.05, 0.2]), 'btn': BIG, 'wind': WIND1, 'door': [6.1, 2.2, -1.5]}, margin=0.16, top=0.12, bottom=0.74)
C1 = cam(0.0, F1, add(F1, [0.12, 0.05, -0.15]), L1, L1, lens=LN1, ease='inOut')
chk2('S01', C1, {'head': add(H1, [0, 2.35, 0]), 'feet': H1, 'btn': BIG, 'wind': WIND1}, heads=('head',))
HK1 = [k(-0.5, look='camera'), k(0.0, toon={**HAND(WIND1, None, 'open'), 'sq': [0.95, 1.06, 0.95], 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.4}}, toonDur=0.0),
       k(r(SLAP1 - 0.07), toon={**HAND(add(HIT1, [0.05, 0.12, 0.05]), None, 'open', hose=0.1), 'sq': [1.03, 0.98, 1.03], 'face': {**HF, 'lid': 0.1}}, toonDur=0.06, toonEase='in'),
       k(SLAP1, toon={**HAND(HIT1, None, 'open', tipR=0.1), 'sq': [1.14, 0.86, 1.14], 'hairUp': 0.9, 'face': SPLAT_FACE(mouth='o')}, toonDur=0.03),
       k(r(SLAP1 + 0.1), toon={**HAND(HIT1, None, 'open', tipR=0.1), 'sq': [0.95, 1.06, 0.95], 'hairUp': 0.4, 'face': {**HF, 'brow': 0.6}}, toonDur=0.07),
       k(r(SLAP1 + 0.22), toon={'sq': [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], 'hip': 0, 'face': HFD}, toonDur=0.1),
       k(r(GO1 - 0.14), toon={'sq': [1.16, 0.82, 1.16], 'hip': 0, 'bend': {'spine': [0.35, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': HFD, 'auto': 0}, toonDur=0.08),
       k(r(GO1 - 0.14), face=-68, turn=0.08),
       k(GO1, to=[1.2, G, 0.75], dur=0.34, ease='linear', clip='run', face=-68),
       k(GO1, toon={'sq': [0.86, 1.2, 0.86], 'hip': 0, 'bend': {'spine': [0.4, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': HFD, 'smear': 0.7}, toonDur=0.05)]
st.shot('S01', SET, setOpts=SETO, look=LOOK_IN, dark=[[0, 1, 0.0], [SLAP1, 0, 0.0]], **DARK,
        actors=[act('mec', H1, RY1, 'stand', 'neutral', keys=HK1)],
        props=[WELL('1', lit=[[0, 0], [SLAP1, 1]], top=2), BTNS('1', press=[[0, SLAP1]], floors=[0, 1, 2]), LINES('1', on=0.0, off_=SLAP1, top=2), BRIEF('1'),
               P('trou1', 'mnGhost', pos=H1, ry=RY1 + 55, opts={'at': r(GO1 + 0.06), 'dir': -1, 'dur': 0.6})],
        cams=[C1])
GAG('S01', SLAP1, 'mec', 'slaps the front-door button'); GAG('S01', r(GO1 - 0.1), 'mec', 'crouch, determined')
st.cue('clack', 'S01', SLAP1, 0.5); st.cue('sfx:click', 'S01', r(SLAP1 + 0.02), 0.3); st.cue('whoosh', 'S01', GO1, 0.25, 0.35, 500, 2600)

# 1b: « La minuterie dure trente secondes. » Up the stairwell from the foot of the well: the flights and landings stacked like a telescope, the top one
#     tiny; the camera rises and turns slowly; low in a corner, the first landing's orange button glows (the running gag starts, never said); his
#     footsteps race up
D1b = st.dur('S01b')
# (the camera has no roll, so the zenith, where the landings converge, stays on the frame's middle line: the column of buttons runs from the first
# landing's, low on the right, up toward it, small glows on a pale column, off the middle; S16 centres them and makes them big)
F1b = [-0.9, 1.15, 0.38]; L1b = [2.37, 10.49, -1.08]
C1b = cam(0.0, F1b, add(F1b, [0.0, 0.4, 0.0]), L1b, add(L1b, [0.0, 0.4, 0.25]), lens=56, ease='inOut')
chk2('S01b', C1b, {'btn0': BTN(0), 'btn1': BTN(1), 'btn2': BTN(2), 'btn3': BTN(3), 'top': [0, 22.0, 0]})
st.shot('S01b', SET, setOpts=SETO, look=LOOK_IN, actors=[],
        props=[WELL('1b', front=True), BTNS('1b', glow=0.55, size=0.85)], cams=[C1b])
GAG('S01b', 0.5, 'mec', 'the telescope of landings')
for i_ in range(6): st.cue('sfx:stepRun', 'S01b', r(0.08 + 0.16 * i_), 0.18)
st.cue('sfx:ticks', 'S01b', 0.55, 0.12)

# ============================== the neighbour du troisième (tiny, grey bun, purple coat, tartan trolley): she presses the button of every landing with one
# finger, deadpan, always in her own light; on a landing she stands by the newel column, the trolley behind her
VNOD = {**VF, 'lid': 0.5}
# walking with the trolley: her left mitten held behind her in her own frame (a world point would stay behind as she walks); the trolley follows by keys
VTT = {'touch': {'L': ['torso', 0.24, 0.12, -0.36, 1, 0.0]}, 'hands': {'L': 'grip', 'R': 'rest'}, 'hip': 0}
def VSTAND(p, ry, trolley_at=None, press=None, t_press=None, other=None):
    # her pose by the column: the left mitten on the trolley's handle, the right one at rest (or pressing BTN(press) at t_press)
    tp = trolley_at or off(p, ry, -0.5, -0.32)
    hd = handle(tp, yaw(tp, p))
    return tp, hd
def PRESS_KEYS(p, ry, k_, t0, hd, face=VF, dur=0.5):
    # one finger up to the button and back, without looking (her eyes stay ahead); a tiny rise on her toes at the press
    B = add(BTN(k_), [0.0, 0.0, 0.03])
    rest = HAND(None, hd, 'rest', 'grip')
    up = HAND(add(B, [0.12, -0.08, 0.08]), hd, 'point', 'grip', tipR=0.15, hose=0.12)
    push = HAND(B, hd, 'point', 'grip', tipR=0.15, hose=0.12)
    return [k(r(t0 - 0.22), toon={**up, 'face': face}, toonDur=0.16, toonEase='inOut'),
            k(r(t0 - 0.02), toon={**push, 'sq': [0.97, 1.04, 0.97], 'face': face}, toonDur=0.05),
            k(r(t0 + 0.12), toon={**push, 'face': face}, toonDur=0.05),
            k(r(t0 + 0.22), toon={**up, 'face': face}, toonDur=0.08),
            k(r(t0 + dur), toon={**rest, 'face': face}, toonDur=0.2, toonEase='inOut')]

